b92c1b4a7a58164a198e.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/57\\/ed1f11ead4b92c1b4a7a58164a198e\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cy13\\/cw414\\/ch414\\/images\\/uploads\\/57ed1f11ead4b92c1b4a7a58164a198e.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":\"\",\"search_text\":\"Trapped within the four walls of a university bedroom, our title character navigates the euphoric highs and crushing lows of Freshers week, toxic friendships, club culture, and the aching need for connection.\\u00a0Monkeyface is the bold, debut play by writer-performer Raphael Phillips, that journeys through the themes of racism, mental health, and loneliness.\\u00a0\\u00a0Content warnings\\u00a0This show contains strong language and references to drug use, as well as themes of mental health, racism, and sexual content throughout.\\u00a0People under the age of 16 are not permitted for this show.\\u00a0Latecomers will not be admitted for this show.\\u00a0Director - Mojola AkinyemiStage Manager & Lighting Designer: Jessica SpellerSound Designer: Joe HarringtonProducer: Emmanuel Akwafo\",\"book_link\":false,\"search\":\"Monkeyface Monkeyface   <p>Trapped within the four walls of a university bedroom, our title character navigates the euphoric highs and crushing lows of Freshers week, toxic friendships, club culture, and the aching need for connection.&nbsp;<\\/p><p><i><strong>Monkeyface <\\/strong><\\/i>is the bold, debut play by writer-performer Raphael Phillips, that journeys through the themes of racism, mental health, and loneliness.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Content warnings&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p>This show contains strong language and references to drug use, as well as themes of mental health, racism, and sexual content throughout.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>People under the age of 16 are not permitted for this show.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Latecomers will not be admitted for this show.&nbsp;<\\/p><p><br><strong>Director<\\/strong> - Mojola Akinyemi<br><br><strong>Stage Manager &amp; Lighting Designer<\\/strong>: Jessica Speller<br><br><strong>Sound Designer: <\\/strong>Joe Harrington<br><br><strong>Producer: <\\/strong>Emmanuel Akwafo<\\/p> Monkeyface  Trapped within the four walls of a university bedroom, our title character navigates the euphoric highs and crushing lows of Freshers week, toxic friendships, club culture, and the aching need for connection.\\u00a0Monkeyface is the bold, debut play by writer-performer Raphael Phillips, that journeys through the themes of racism, mental health, and loneliness.\\u00a0\\u00a0Content warnings\\u00a0This show contains strong language and references to drug use, as well as themes of mental health, racism, and sexual content throughout.\\u00a0People under the age of 16 are not permitted for this show.\\u00a0Latecomers will not be admitted for this show.\\u00a0Director - Mojola AkinyemiStage Manager & Lighting Designer: Jessica SpellerSound Designer: Joe HarringtonProducer: Emmanuel Akwafo\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/1k-kill-bill-the-whole-bloody-affair\\/\",\"id\":\"597\",\"name\":\"Kill Bill: The Whole Bloody Affair\",\"title\":\"Kill Bill: The Whole Bloody Affair\",\"duration\":\"241 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1768003200\":[{\"tag_ids\":[],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/21404\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">12:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1768046400\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1768089600\":[{\"tag_ids\":[],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/14651\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">13:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1768136400\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1768003200,1768089600],\"start_date\":\"176804640